musthear","grp":null,"list_year":null,"rank":596,"year":null,"note":null,"total":877,"scaruffi":null}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"By the release of this album in 1983, New Order had fully committed to a dance floor-oriented sound, marking a pivotal moment in their musical evolution. Their embrace of electronic elements and complex rhythms was evident throughout the record. \"by the time they released their power, corruption, and lies album in 1983, they were all in when it came to the dance floor.\"","year":1983,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The Post-Punk Explosion Part 4: Alt-Dance","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0FYq5MBdHw4"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"This album is seen as the point where New Order became a completely different band. Critics praised it, recognizing New Order's entirely new musical path within the United Kingdom. \"Y luego ya es en 1983, yo creo que cuando sale Power Corruption and Lies. Donde ya es un New Order completamente diferente, me refiero con Power Corruption and Lies, la crítica se deshacen a la Wisconsin New Order, y ahora, en un camino totalmente nuevo, musicalmente dentro del reino nido.\"","year":1983,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"Especial JOY DIVISION: 4. La banda tras el final","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r5DddiWrUbA"}]}],"book_tracks":[{"id":164489415082574,"artist":"New Order","artist_id":80644305471953,"title":"Power, Corruption & Lies","year":1983,"ess":0,"yt":"A3Pm1f4koNc","kind":null,"book":{"id":7,"title":"Postpunk. Romper todo y empezar de nuevo","author":"Simon Reynolds","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/Postpunk/"},"scene":"New Order","scene_id":80644305471953,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/Postpunk/#new-order","chapters":["Cap. 16: Mutant disco y punk funk: tráfico urbano en Nueva York a principios de los ochenta (y más allá)"],"pages":[]},{"id":164489415082574,"artist":"New Or